==============================================================================
EXPERIMENT GRID  (24 h horizon, 12 h warm-up excluded)
seeds=6  workers=8  quick=False
==============================================================================

[E4] Downgrade-forcing cost k*(phi) vs relay-chain depth
    -> results/e4_forcing_cost.csv  (624 rows)

  k*(phi) = minimum links the adversary must suppress to FORCE a
  fraction phi of ENTITLED sessions (authorised floor >= G2) below an
  information-theoretically delivered key. Measured on forced
  degradation, not raw below-ITS: LOG traffic is authorised at G3, so
  counting it would credit the adversary before it acted.

  --- adversary targeting: betweenness ---
  depth links  nominal   k*(0.1)  k*(0.25)   k*(0.5)
      1     1    0.000         1         1         1
      2     5    0.000         3         3         3
      3     7    0.000         4         4         4
      4     9    0.000         1         5         5
      5    11    0.000         1         6         6
      6    13    0.000         1         7         7

  --- adversary targeting: mincut ---
  depth links  nominal   k*(0.1)  k*(0.25)   k*(0.5)
      1     1    0.000         1         1         1
      2     5    0.000         1         2         2
      3     7    0.000         1         2         2
      4     9    0.000         1         2         2
      5    11    0.000         1         2         2
      6    13    0.000         1         2         2

  A betweenness-guided adversary exhausts the already-severed
  primary path before touching the alternate; the min-cut adversary
  does not. The gap IS the finding: reporting only the greedy figure
  overstates resilience by a factor growing in chain depth.
    -> results/e4_kstar.csv  (12 rows)

total wall time: 434.6 s
